<div class="header-badge">FamilyRoots System Architecture &bull; Events Full CRUD Guide</div>
<h1>Family Events Full CRUD &amp; Pagination Architecture</h1>

<p><strong>Platform:</strong> FamilyRoots Digital Sanctuary &bull; Next.js 16 + NestJS 11 + Prisma ORM 7 + PostgreSQL<br>
<strong>Target Modules:</strong> <code>/family/events</code> (Backend) &amp; <code>EventsTab.tsx</code> / <code>familyApi.ts</code> (Frontend)<br>
<strong>Scope of Delivery:</strong> Full CRUD (Create, Read with Pagination/Search, Read by ID, Update, Delete) with complete frontend integration and Swagger documentation.<br>
<strong>Verification Date:</strong> September 25, 2026</p>

<div class="callout-success">
  <strong>Delivery Assurance:</strong> All 5 endpoints for Family Events are fully implemented, verified with unit checks, compiled without errors in both backend and frontend, and documented with explicit role permissions in Swagger and Word specifications.
</div>

<h2>1. Family Events API Endpoint Specifications</h2>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>HTTP Method</th>
      <th>Route Path</th>
      <th>Query / Parameters</th>
      <th>Summary &amp; Purpose</th>
      <th>Allowed Roles</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="http-get">GET</span></td>
      <td><code>/family/events</code></td>
      <td><code>page, limit, search, q, isVirtual, sortBy, sortOrder</code></td>
      <td>Retrieves paginated celebrations and reunions matching keyword search across title, location, and description with total count and page metadata.</td>
      <td><code>MEMBER, USER, OWNER, ADMIN, SUPER_ADMIN</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="http-get">GET</span></td>
      <td><code>/family/events/:id</code></td>
      <td><code>id: string</code> (Path parameter)</td>
      <td>Retrieves complete celebration record, date, venue, agenda, and sanctuary metadata by unique ID.</td>
      <td><code>MEMBER, USER, OWNER, ADMIN, SUPER_ADMIN</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="http-post">POST</span></td>
      <td><code>/family/events</code></td>
      <td><code>CreateEventDto</code> (title, date, location, description, isVirtual)</td>
      <td>Schedules a new celebration or reunion in the sanctuary calendar with venue or online video call URL.</td>
      <td><code>MEMBER, USER, OWNER, ADMIN, SUPER_ADMIN</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="http-patch">PATCH</span></td>
      <td><code>/family/events/:id</code></td>
      <td><code>id: string</code> &amp; <code>UpdateEventDto</code></td>
      <td>Updates event schedule, title, venue, agenda details, or virtual attendance toggle.</td>
      <td><code>MEMBER, USER, OWNER, ADMIN, SUPER_ADMIN</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="http-delete">DELETE</span></td>
      <td><code>/family/events/:id</code></td>
      <td><code>id: string</code> (Path parameter)</td>
      <td>Permanently cancels and deletes an event from the family calendar.</td>
      <td><code>OWNER, ADMIN, SUPER_ADMIN</code> strictly</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>2. Frontend Integration Details (Next.js &amp; RTK Query)</h2>

<h3>2.1. Redux API Client (<code>src/redux/api/familyApi.ts</code>)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><code>useGetEventsQuery({ page, limit, search })</code>: Sends URL search parameters and receives a structured paginated envelope <code>{ data: EventRecord[], meta: PaginationMeta }</code>.</li>
  <li><code>useGetEventByIdQuery(id)</code>: Fetches individual event details with cache key tag <code>{ type: "Events", id }</code>.</li>
  <li><code>useAddEventMutation()</code>: Schedules a new event and invalidates <code>["Sanctuary", "Events"]</code>.</li>
  <li><code>useUpdateEventMutation()</code>: Updates an event and invalidates <code>["Sanctuary", "Events"]</code>.</li>
  <li><code>useDeleteEventMutation()</code>: Deletes an event and invalidates <code>["Sanctuary", "Events"]</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2.2. Interactive Event Components (<code>src/components/dashboard/tabs/EventsTab.tsx</code>)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Live Synced Search &amp; Pagination:</strong> Search input with instant query debouncing, clear filter button, and pagination controls (Previous/Next page, Limit picker).</li>
  <li><strong>Event Details Modal (<code>EventDetailsModal</code>):</strong> Opens when clicking "Details" (Eye icon). Shows full date badge, title, location/URL with copy button, full agenda description, sanctuary name, and action triggers.</li>
  <li><strong>Edit Event Modal (<code>EditEventModal</code>):</strong> Opens when clicking "Edit" (Pencil icon). Form allows modifying title, date, venue, description, and virtual flag with instant validation and feedback.</li>
  <li><strong>Delete Action:</strong> Trash button with confirmation modal/prompt, automatically removing the item and updating the UI instantly.</li>
  <li><strong>Creation Modal (<code>AddEventModal.tsx</code>):</strong> Upgraded with responsive centered layout and full description/agenda support.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Event Lifecycle &amp; Automatic Active/Inactive Status Logic</h2>
<p>To provide immediate visual clarity on event timeliness, an automated lifecycle status calculation has been added across the full stack:</p>

<div class="callout-info">
  <strong>Status Determination Rule:</strong>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>ACTIVE (Upcoming / Scheduled):</strong> Evaluated when <code>eventDate &gt;= today</code> (at midnight boundary). Indicates an upcoming or ongoing celebration scheduled for today or any future date.</li>
    <li><strong>INACTIVE (Expired / Past Event):</strong> Evaluated when <code>eventDate &lt; today</code>. Indicates that the celebration date has passed and the event is archived/expired.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<h3>Full Stack Implementation Features:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Server-Side Auto-Enrichment:</strong> <code>EventsService</code> automatically computes and attaches <code>status: 'ACTIVE' | 'INACTIVE'</code> to every event returned by <code>getEvents</code>, <code>getEventById</code>, <code>createEvent</code>, and <code>updateEvent</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Server-Side Status Filtering:</strong> <code>GET /family/events?status=ACTIVE</code> filters events on or after today, while <code>?status=INACTIVE</code> filters past events.</li>
  <li><strong>Interactive Status Filter Pills:</strong> The top action bar provides quick tabs: <em>All Events</em>, <em>Active (Upcoming)</em>, and <em>Inactive (Expired)</em>.</li>
  <li><strong>Visual Event Card Badges:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Active Badge:</strong> Glowing emerald badge with pulsating green indicator (<code>&bull; Active</code>) and vibrant emerald calendar date badge.</li>
      <li><strong>Inactive Badge:</strong> Clean slate/muted badge (<code>&bull; Inactive</code>) with muted calendar square, instantly distinguishing past celebrations.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Live Date Picker Preview:</strong> In both <code>AddEventModal</code> and <code>EditEventModal</code>, picking a date immediately renders a live preview indicator (<em>Status: Active (Upcoming)</em> or <em>Status: Inactive (Expired / Past)</em>) before submitting.</li>
  <li><strong>Comprehensive Event Details Modal:</strong> Displays both the active/inactive badge and an explicit Lifecycle Status row in the metadata panel.</li>
</ul>

